le, if I have 10 customers whose orders are. The console will introduce the user and prompt the user to enter X number of orders. It will then print out the list of orders in ascending and descending order i.e. using a stack and queue.   If the customer enters \u201cQUIT\u201d the outro will be printed and both lists will be printed to the console.","topics":[],"score":226133,"global_rank":133111},{"name":"fabricekalvanda/SeachAndSort","owner":"fabricekalvanda","html_url":"https://github.com/fabricekalvanda/SeachAndSort","stars":0,"forks":0,"watchers":1,"issues":0,"language":"C#","description":"Given a list of numbers by the user, this program will find the element the user is searching for.","topics":[],"score":226133,"global_rank":133112},{"name":"fabricekalvanda/shapes","owner":"fabricekalvanda","html_url":"https://github.com/fabricekalvanda/shapes","stars":0,"forks":0,"watchers":1,"issues":0,"language":"C#","description":"I have multiple shapes. Each shape does something different depending on what it is.","topics":[],"score":226133,"global_rank":133113},{"name":"fabricekalvanda/quilts","owner":"fabricekalvanda","html_url":"https://github.com/fabricekalvanda/quilts","stars":0,"forks":0,"watchers":1,"issues":0,"language":"C#","description":"I have a business that sells quilts of the same pattern, but different sizes depending on the customers needs. A customer is able to request a quilt with this pattern as big as they want.","topics":[],"score":226133,"global_rank":133114},{"name":"fabricekalvanda/diceGame","owner":"fabricekalvanda","html_url":"https://github.com/fabricekalvanda/diceGame","stars":0,"forks":0,"watchers":1,"issues":0,"language":"C#","description":"I have 2 die, 6 sided each I start the game and print the intro  \u201cHey! Welcome to Tina\u2019s Dice Game.\u201d \u201cLet\u2019s start!\u201d The computer randomly generates what side of the die is chosen (for each die) I then add both of the random numbers together  I then print  Dice 1 = (the random number I got)  Dice 2 = (the random number I got) Depending on what number I get, something different is printed to the screen If I get an even number  I print \u201cI got (value of dice 1) and (value of dice 2)!\u201d  I print \u201cEvens are better than odds!\u201d If I get an odd number I print \u201cI got (value of dice 1) and (value of dice 2)!\u201d  I print \u201cOdds are still cool!\u201d At the end, I ask the user if they want to play again If the answer is \u201cYES\u201d  I \u201cthrow\u201d the die again and repeat the printing process If the answer is anything but YES (case-sensitive) I end the game and print the outro  \u201cThe number of times the dice was thrown is: (value of times dice is thrown)\u201d \u201cNice game!\u201d \u201cThanks for playing, Come play again soon!\u201d\u2028","topics":[],"score":226133,"global_rank":133115},{"name":"GregBahm/PokerVis","owner":"GregBahm","html_url":"https://github.com/GregBahm/PokerVis","stars":0,"forks":1,"watchers":0,"issues":0,"language":"C#","description":"Visualize the win probabilities of poker hands","topics":[],"score":226130,"global_rank":133237},{"name":"Zirkander/python_bands","owner":"Zirkander","html_url":"https://github.com/Zirkander/python_bands","stars":0,"forks":0,"watchers":1,"issues":0,"language":"C#","description":null,"topics":[],"score":226122,"global_rank":133266},{"name":"arthur-ryoo/.NetCoreQuestionsApp","owner":"arthur-ryoo","html_url":"https://github.com/arthur-ryoo/.NetCoreQuestionsApp","stars":0,"forks":0,"watchers":1,"issues":0,"language":"C#","description":"A web database app in ASP.NET Core.","topics":[],"score":226119,"global_rank":133328},{"name":"ahmelsayed/scaler-example","owner":"ahmelsayed","html_url":"https://github.com/ahmelsayed/scaler-example","stars":0,"forks":0,"watchers":1,"issues":0,"language":"C#","description":null,"topics":[],"score":226109,"global_rank":133475},{"name":"PortableTomb/NodeJumper","owner":"PortableTomb","html_url":"https://github.com/PortableT